Keeps `public/` present in git.

Next's standalone output expects this directory to exist — the
Dockerfile does `COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public`, which fails
the image build if it is missing. PR #148 deleted the last file in here
(five unreferenced create-next-app boilerplate SVGs), and because git
does not track empty directories the folder vanished from the repo and
the next image build broke.

Delete this file only when a real public asset (favicon, robots.txt,
og-image) takes its place.
